// Prints: 2</code></pre><p class="codeend">End of code.</p></div><p>A <code>TypeError</code> will be thrown if <code>arrayBuffer</code> is not an <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/ArrayBuffer">ArrayBuffer</a> or a
<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/SharedArrayBuffer">SharedArrayBuffer</a> or another type appropriate for <code>Buffer.from()</code>
variants.</p><p>It is important to remember that a backing <code>ArrayBuffer</code> can cover a range
of memory that extends beyond the bounds of a <code>TypedArray</code> view. A new
