<section><h3 id="consolelogdata-args"><code>console.log([data][, ...args])</code><a id="console_console_log_data_args"></a></h3><div class="api_metadata">Added in: v0.1.100</div><ul>
<li><code>data</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Data_types">any</a>)</li>
<li><code>...args</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Data_types">any</a>)</li>
</ul><p>Prints to <code>stdout</code> with newline. Multiple arguments can be passed, with the
first used as the primary message and all additional used as substitution
values similar to <a href="http://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/printf.3.html"><code>printf(3)</code></a> (the arguments are all passed to <a href="#utilformatformat-args"><code>util.format()</code></a>).</p><div class="codeblock"><p class="codelabel">Code example:</p><pre><code>const count = 5;
console.log('count: %d', count);
