<li><code>name</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#string_type">string</a>): The name of the requested lock resource.</li>
<li><code>mode</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#string_type">string</a>): The lock mode: <code>'exclusive'</code> or <code>'shared'</code>.</li>
<li><code>steal</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#boolean_type">boolean</a>): Whether the request uses steal semantics.</li>
<li><code>ifAvailable</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#boolean_type">boolean</a>): Whether the request uses ifAvailable semantics.</li>
<li><code>error</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Error">Error</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#undefined_type">undefined</a>): The error thrown by the callback, if any.</li>
</ul><p>Emitted when a lock request has finished, whether the callback succeeded,
threw an error, or the lock was stolen.</p></section>
