<section><h3 id="err_package_map_external_file"><code>ERR_PACKAGE_MAP_EXTERNAL_FILE</code><a id="errors_err_package_map_external_file"></a></h3><div class="api_metadata">Added in: v26.4.0</div><p>A module attempted to resolve a bare specifier using the <a href="#package-maps">package map</a>, but
the importing file is not located within any package defined in the map.</p><div class="codeblock"><p class="codelabel">Code example:</p><pre><code>$ node --experimental-package-map=./package-map.json /tmp/script.js
Error [ERR_PACKAGE_MAP_EXTERNAL_FILE]: Cannot resolve "dep-a" from "/tmp/script.js": file is not within any package defined in /path/to/package-map.json</code></pre><p class="codeend">End of code.</p></div><p>To fix this error, ensure the importing file is inside one of the package
directories listed in the package map, or add a new package entry whose <code>url</code>
covers the importing file.</p><p><a id="ERR_PACKAGE_MAP_INVALID"></a></p></section>
<section><h3 id="err_package_map_invalid"><code>ERR_PACKAGE_MAP_INVALID</code><a id="errors_err_package_map_invalid"></a></h3><div class="api_metadata">Added in: v26.4.0</div><p>The <a href="#package-maps">package map</a> configuration file is invalid. This can occur when:</p><ul>
<li>The file does not exist at the specified path.</li>
<li>The file contains invalid JSON.</li>
<li>The file is missing the required <code>packages</code> object.</li>
<li>A package entry is missing the required <code>url</code> field.</li>
<li>Two package entries have the same <code>url</code> value.</li>
</ul><div class="codeblock"><p class="codelabel">Code example:</p><pre><code>$ node --experimental-package-map=./missing.json app.js
Error [ERR_PACKAGE_MAP_INVALID]: Invalid package map at "./missing.json": file not found</code></pre><p class="codeend">End of code.</p></div><p><a id="ERR_PACKAGE_MAP_KEY_NOT_FOUND"></a></p></section>
<section><h3 id="err_package_map_key_not_found"><code>ERR_PACKAGE_MAP_KEY_NOT_FOUND</code><a id="errors_err_package_map_key_not_found"></a></h3><div class="api_metadata">Added in: v26.4.0</div><p>A package's <code>dependencies</code> object in the <a href="#package-maps">package map</a> references a package
key that is not defined in the <code>packages</code> object.</p><div class="codeblock"><p class="codelabel">Code example:</p><pre><code>{
  "packages": {
    "app": {
      "url": "./app",
      "dependencies": {
        "foo": "nonexistent"
      }
    }
  }
}</code></pre><p class="codeend">End of code.</p></div><p>In this example, <code>"nonexistent"</code> is referenced as a dependency target but not
defined in <code>packages</code>, which will throw this error.</p><p>To fix this error, ensure all package keys referenced in <code>dependencies</code> values
are defined in the <code>packages</code> object.</p><p><a id="ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED"></a></p></section>
<section><h3 id="err_package_path_not_exported"><code>ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED</code><a id="errors_err_package_path_not_exported"></a></h3><div class="api_metadata"></div><p>The <code>package.json</code> <a href="#packages--exports"><code>"exports"</code></a> field does not export the requested subpath.
Because exports are encapsulated, private internal modules that are not exported
cannot be imported through the package resolution, unless using an absolute URL.</p><p><a id="ERR_PARSE_ARGS_INVALID_OPTION_VALUE"></a></p></section>
<section><h3 id="err_parse_args_invalid_option_value"><code>ERR_PARSE_ARGS_INVALID_OPTION_VALUE</code><a id="errors_err_parse_args_invalid_option_value"></a></h3><div class="api_metadata">Added in: v18.3.0, v16.17.0</div><p>When <code>strict</code> set to <code>true</code>, thrown by <a href="#utilparseargsconfig"><code>util.parseArgs()</code></a> if a <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#boolean_type">boolean</a>
value is provided for an option of type <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#string_type">string</a>, or if a <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#string_type">string</a>
value is provided for an option of type <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#boolean_type">boolean</a>.</p><p><a id="ERR_PARSE_ARGS_UNEXPECTED_POSITIONAL"></a></p></section>
