<li><code>buffer</code> (<a href="#buffer--class-buffer">Buffer</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/TypedArray">TypedArray</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/DataView">DataView</a>)</li>
<li><code>offset</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">integer</a>)</li>
<li><code>length</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">integer</a>)</li>
<li><code>position</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">integer</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#bigint_type">bigint</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#null_type">null</a>): <strong>Default:</strong> <code>null</code></li>
<li>Returns: <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">number</a></li>
</ul><p>Returns the number of <code>bytesRead</code>.</p><p>For detailed information, see the documentation of the asynchronous version of
this API: <a href="#fsreadfd-buffer-offset-length-position-callback"><code>fs.read()</code></a>.</p></section>
<section><h3 id="fsreadsyncfd-buffer-options"><code>fs.readSync(fd, buffer[, options])</code><a id="fs_fs_readsync_fd_buffer_options"></a></h3><div class="api_metadata">Added in: v13.13.0, v12.17.0<div class="changelog"><p class="histlabel">History</p><table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Changes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>v13.13.0, v12.17.0</td><td><p>Options object can be passed in to make offset, length, and position optional.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><ul>
<li><code>fd</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">integer</a>)</li>
<li><code>buffer</code> (<a href="#buffer--class-buffer">Buffer</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/TypedArray">TypedArray</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/DataView">DataView</a>)</li>
<li><code>options</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object">Object</a>)
<ul>
<li><code>offset</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">integer</a>): <strong>Default:</strong> <code>0</code></li>
<li><code>length</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">integer</a>): <strong>Default:</strong> <code>buffer.byteLength - offset</code></li>
<li><code>position</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">integer</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#bigint_type">bigint</a> or <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#null_type">null</a>): <strong>Default:</strong> <code>null</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Returns: <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#number_type">number</a></li>
</ul><p>Returns the number of <code>bytesRead</code>.</p><p>Similar to the above <code>fs.readSync</code> function, this version takes an optional <code>options</code> object.
