<li><code>flush</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#boolean_type">boolean</a>): If all data is successfully written to the file, and <code>flush</code> is <code>true</code>, <code>fs.fsyncSync()</code> is used to flush the data.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Returns: <code>undefined</code>.</li>
</ul><p>The <code>mode</code> option only affects the newly created file. See <a href="#fsopenpath-flags-mode-callback"><code>fs.open()</code></a>
for more details.</p><p>For detailed information, see the documentation of the asynchronous version of
this API: <a href="#fswritefilefile-data-options-callback"><code>fs.writeFile()</code></a>.</p></section>
