<section><h2 id="class-abortcontroller">Class: <code>AbortController</code><a id="globals_class_abortcontroller"></a></h2><div class="api_metadata">Added in: v15.0.0, v14.17.0<div class="changelog"><p class="histlabel">History</p><table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Changes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>v15.4.0</td><td><p>No longer experimental.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p>A utility class used to signal cancelation in selected <code>Promise</code>-based APIs.
The API is based on the Web API <a href="#class-abortcontroller">AbortController</a>.</p><div class="codeblock"><p class="codelabel">Code example:</p><pre><code>const ac = new AbortController();

ac.signal.addEventListener('abort', () => console.log('Aborted!'),
                           { once: true });

ac.abort();

console.log(ac.signal.aborted);  // Prints true</code></pre><p class="codeend">End of code.</p></div></section>
<section><h3 id="abortcontrollerabortreason"><code>abortController.abort([reason])</code><a id="globals_abortcontroller_abort_reason"></a></h3><div class="api_metadata">Added in: v15.0.0, v14.17.0<div class="changelog"><p class="histlabel">History</p><table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Changes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>v17.2.0, v16.14.0</td><td><p>Added the new optional reason argument.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><ul>
<li><code>reason</code> (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/JavaScript/Data_structures#Data_types">any</a>): An optional reason, retrievable on the <code>AbortSignal</code>'s
<code>reason</code> property.</li>
</ul><p>Triggers the abort signal, causing the <code>abortController.signal</code> to emit
the <code>'abort'</code> event.</p></section>
